// A stray block end in the main source file, rather than in an included one.
//
// module-include-eof is the same condition reached through 'include', and it
// was diagnosed while this was not: of the three callers of the global-
// statement parser, parsePgm was the one with no end-of-file check. So a '}'
// at global scope ended the statement loop and everything after it was
// discarded in silence -- no diagnostic, exit 0, an object file emitted from
// half the source. The declaration below the stray brace is here to be the
// half that used to vanish.
//
// The diagnostic is reported at the token that should have followed the file,
// which is that declaration's first token, so the annotation sits on it.

fn beforeTheStrayBlockEnd(n i64) i64 {
  n
}

}

fn afterTheStrayBlockEnd(n i64) i64 {   //~ ErrorNoEof:1 "Expected end-of-file"
  n
}
